course: dictionary
lesson: 13357
title: Hank: a loop of wool or a name
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A hank is a loose loop or coil of wool, yarn, thread, rope or hair, wound and tied so it does not tangle. «Mum bought a hank of blue wool for our knitting club.» The words wool and knitting are your clues: a hank is a bundle of yarn you can use to make something.
explain: Before you knit, you often need to wind a hank into a ball. «Ava wound the hank into a ball before she started her scarf.» Check your meaning: if you swap in "a loop of wool", the sentence still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Hank is also a name, with a capital H. «Hank, my cousin from Texas, plays the guitar.» Here Hank is a person, not a bundle of wool. Hank is a short form of Henry, and you will meet it often in American stories and films.
fact: A hank is a noun. One is a hank, and more than one is hanks.
fact: «Hank» means a loop or coil of wool, yarn, thread, rope or hair, loosely wound and tied.
fact: «A hank of hair» means a thick lock of hair.
fact: Hank is also a man's first name, a short form of Henry, mostly used in the USA.
fact: When Hank is a name, it always starts with a capital letter.
exercise: «Mum bought a hank of blue wool.» What is a hank? | *A loop of wool, loosely wound and tied | A pair of knitting needles | A ball of cake mix
exercise: «Hank, my cousin from Texas, plays the guitar.» In this sentence, what kind of word is Hank? | A bundle of wool | A type of hair | *A name | A colour
exercise: «Her hank of hair fell across her face.» What does hank mean here? | *A thick lock of hair | A short, sharp pull | A type of hat | A hair clip
test: Which sentence uses Hank as a name? | «She tied the hank with string.» | «The wool came in a hank.» | *«Hank called to say hello from Texas.» | «A hank of rope lay on the deck.»
test: What do you usually do to a hank of wool before knitting? | *Wind it into a ball | Eat it | Freeze it | Paint it
exam: Which word best completes this sentence? «Ava wound the ___ of yarn into a ball before knitting.» | bridge | whistle | cake | *hank
